<BaseLayout
  title="Android Kotlin SDK Docs — TesterLoop"
  description="Integrate TesterLoop SDK into native Android apps in 2 deterministic steps with zero Kotlin code."
  canonicalPath="/docs/sdk/android"
>
  <article class="card">
    <h1>TesterLoop Android SDK (Kotlin / Java)</h1>
    <p>Zero runtime code required. Auto-initializes via <code>androidx.startup</code>.</p>

    <h2>1. Add dependency (<code>app/build.gradle.kts</code>)</h2>
    <pre><code>dependencies &#123;
    implementation("io.testerloop:sdk:1.0.0")
&#125;</code></pre>

    <h2>2. Add APP_KEY meta-data (<code>app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml</code>)</h2>
    <pre><code>&lt;meta-data
    android:name="io.testerloop.APP_KEY"
    android:value="tl_pk_your_app_key_here" /&gt;</code></pre>

    <p>AI assistants can read <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a> directly.</p>
  </article>
